id: ops-input-startup-timeout
title: Separate artifact-reader startup time from the bounded input-refusal deadline
description: "The unchanged special-input regression in test/regular-input.test.ts hit its five-second child timeout in a two-worker full gate and an isolated one-worker retry. The npm serial full gate and PR CI passed unchanged. Its child imports the full SDK, package extension and all input consumers before exercising the input boundary, so the deadline includes cold startup. A diagnostic measured about 3.5 seconds of imports before the first refusal assertion; a full successful phase trace is still being collected. Do not infer a blocked FIFO read from the timeout alone."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T03:42:57.531Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-20T13:16:00.423Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Measure child readiness and input-refusal execution separately with bounded deadlines; Preserve real writerless FIFO, socket, device, directory and oversized-file assertions without weakening coverage thresholds; Demonstrate stable cold-start behavior under bounded test concurrency"
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T03:44:19.100Z",codex-agent,"Control evidence from the unchanged test: unrestricted one-worker execution passed 6/6, and a subsequent one-worker run on another CPU pair also passed 6/6. A separate real FIFO diagnostic recorded preload-to-import readiness of about 1.5 seconds and all eight typed refusals within roughly 20 milliseconds after readiness; total child wall time was about 1.8 seconds. A prior diagnostic measured about 3.5 seconds of import time. These observations support a startup/load timing risk, while not identifying the exact phase of the killed child. All existing five-second limits and assertions remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T04:00:35.244Z",codex-agent,"The complete one-worker Bun release gate passed unchanged: 1468 passed, 0 failed, 2 opt-in skips, with 100% coverage in every dimension across 39 measured sources. The special-input case passed in that full run. The initial two-worker timeout and isolated timeout remain valid observations; successful retries do not establish load-independent timing. Leave this follow-up open."
  "2026-10-27T10:05:25.444Z",codex-agent,"Closure audit of PR #216 (eac1589d0fd598ae0c5375b4d83806418b86c5e4): passing unchanged release gates do not satisfy this item. Separate child-readiness and refusal deadlines, retained special-input assertions, and cold-start stability still need implementation and measurement. Keep open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-28T16:30:05.432Z",glm-agent,"Observed again while validating the historical-release recovery branch: the unchanged regular-input subprocess test exceeded its existing 5000 ms child limit in a two-worker full release gate. Total test duration was about 10 seconds, including setup; this does not prove a blocked input read. That full run reported 1490 passed, 1 failed, 2 optional configured-repository skips. The timeout prevented assurance.ts and index.ts refusal branches from being counted; release-repair.ts and the new changelog-section verifier each reached 100% across all dimensions. Retrying the reader file separately before the Bun gate; leaving this issue open and unclaimed, with all deadlines and thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-10-28T16:32:42.713Z",glm-agent,"Fresh isolated reproductions during release recovery validation: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/regular-input.test.ts reported 5 passed, 1 failed, 0 skipped on both nvm Node 24.19.0 and nvm Node 26.12.0. The same unchanged 5000 ms special-input child limit timed out; other reader assertions passed. This supports the existing startup/load follow-up but does not identify a blocked input operation. No test deadline or production input code was changed."
  "2026-10-28T16:51:12.003Z",glm-agent,"Additional control evidence: the unchanged full local bun run release:check under nvm Node 26.12.0 subsequently passed 1491 tests, 0 failed, 2 opt-in skips, with 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across 41 measured sources. The special-input test passed in that run. PR #224 CI on the recovery implementation head also passed both npm and Bun gates on Node 22 and 26. The earlier full/isolated timeout observations remain valid; these passes do not establish cold-start stability or separate readiness from refusal execution. Leave this issue open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-28T18:20:24.487Z",glm-agent,"Additional unchanged-test control from PR #224 round 1: Node 26 local npm run release:check passed 1495 tests, 0 failed, 2 opt-in skips with 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across 41 measured sources. The subsequent sequential local bun run release:check hit the existing 5000 ms special-input child-startup limit: 1494 passed, 1 failed, 2 opt-in skips. Total failing test duration was about 10.6 seconds including setup. The newly changed section verifier still measured 100% in all four dimensions; the missed refusal branches were assurance.ts/index.ts, as in earlier controls. No startup deadlines, input-reader code or thresholds were changed. Leave this follow-up open and unclaimed; a successful npm run does not establish cold-start stability."
  "2026-11-20T12:46:03.247Z",codex-sol,"Separate Node boot and imports from the existing five-second input assertion limit. A child readiness handshake will gate the assertions, and the parent will enforce both deadlines and reap a timed-out child. Keep the real special-input cases and run twenty times with four test workers and a CPU-burning sibling."
  "2026-11-20T12:52:03.972Z",codex-sol,"The child now waits for a read instruction after signaling readiness. The parent starts the unchanged 5000 ms refusal watchdog before sending that instruction, kills a timed-out child, and waits for it to close. Startup and shutdown have separate 60 s watchdogs. A scratch probe delaying readiness by 5500 ms passed. A scratch probe that blocks on the writerless FIFO after readiness failed with the 5000 ms refusal diagnostic. The focused Node 22 Linux run passed all 14 reader and runtime tests."
  "2026-11-20T12:57:56.014Z",codex-sol,"A baseline control copied from main reproduced the original external subprocess timeout under node --test --test-concurrency=4 with CPU-burning sibling workers. The same writerless FIFO, socket, devices, directory and oversized file remain covered by the revised test."
  "2026-11-20T13:06:54.887Z",codex-sol,"Stability gate passed 20/20 consecutive Node 24.19.0 runs on a four-core Linux host. Each run used node --test --test-concurrency=4 with the reader test file and three CPU-burning sibling test files. A separate CPU burner ran continuously throughout the loop. Reader tests passed 120/120, including 20/20 full special-input scenarios, with zero failures."
  "2026-11-20T13:15:58.305Z",codex-sol,"The full npm run coverage gate passed on Node 24.19.0 with 1998 passed, zero failed and two opt-in real-data skips. All 50 measured source files met 100% statements, branches, functions and lines. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, duplication and docstring gates passed."
